{"strongs": "H5518", "word": "סִיר", "translit": "sir", "root": "סיר", "morph": "H:N-F", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "pot", "definition": "I. סִיר noun masculine Jer 1:13 and feminine 2Kgs 4:38 pot (probably foreign word (Egyptian ?), Arabic a large water-jar Lane 1276 is perhaps loan-word ; on Greek derivatives σιρός , σίρινος see Lewy Fremdw. 107 ); — ׳ ס absolute 2Kgs 4:38 +, construct Exod 16:3 +; plural סִירֹת Exod 38:3 , סִירוֺת 1Kgs 7:45 +; suffix סִירֹתָיו Exod 27:3 , סִירֹתֵיכֶם Ps 58:10 — pot: 1. a. household utensil for boiling 2Kgs 4:38 ; 2Kgs 4:39 ; 2Kgs 4:40 ; 2Kgs 4:41 (twice in verse) הַבָּשָׂר ׳ ס Exod 16:3 ( P ), Zech 14:21 נָפוּחַ ׳ ס Jer 1:13 (compare נפח in vision), symbolic of Jerusalem Ezek 11:3 ; Ezek 11:7 ; Ezek 11:11 ; Ezek 24:3 ; Ezek 24:6 figurative also Ps 58:10 (compare Che ); in simile Mic 3:3 ; Job 41:23 ; Eccl 7:6 . \\ \\ b. רַחְצִי ׳ ס Ps 60:10 my washing-pot , Ps 108:10 . 2. pots used in sanctuary, Ezek 27:3 ; Ezek 38:3 (both P ), 1Kgs 7:40 (read סִירוֺת for ᵑ0 כִּיִּרוֺת , so Manuscripts of HCT ᵐ5 ᵑ9 Th Ke Klo Kmp Benz ), v 1Kgs 7:45 = 2Chr 4:11 ; 2Chr 4:16 ; 2Kgs 25:14 = Jer 52:18 , also Jer 52:19 ; 2Chr 35:13 ; Zech 14:20 . — Here belongs probably סִרָה in בּוֺר הַסִּרָה .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5570')\">BDB5570</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H5518')\">H5518</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5569')\">BDB5569</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5571')\">BDB5571</entry></div><p> I. <bdbheb>סִיר</bdbheb> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Jer 1:13\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(24,1,13)\">Jer 1:13</ref></sup> and <b>feminine</b><sup><ref ref=\"2Kgs 4:38\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"38\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"38\" onclick=\"bcv(12,4,38)\">2Kgs 4:38</ref></sup> <highlightword>pot</highlightword> (probably foreign word (Egyptian ?), Arabic <placeholder3571/> a large water-jar <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Lan